@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+## Context
+
+`src/pointer.ts` parses RFC 6901 pointers (private `parsePointer`) and resolves them. Patch operations need parsing plus parent lookup, so parsing must be reusable.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:** RFC 6902 behavior, no mutation of inputs, atomic failure.
+**Non-Goals:** JSON Merge Patch, patch generation (diff), in-place application.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Export `parsePointer` from `pointer.ts` (not from `index.ts`) and reuse it, so pointer errors are consistent.
+- Deep-clone the document once up front and mutate the clone; operation values and `copy` sources are cloned as well. Any throw discards the clone, which gives atomicity for free.
+- Walk to the parent of the target via the parsed tokens, requiring each step to exist (own members only, canonical array indices). Member assignment uses `Object.defineProperty` so names such as `__proto__` are plain data.
+- `move` = remove + add after checking `from` is not a proper prefix of `path` (token-wise). `from === path` is a no-op after verifying existence.
+- Equality for `test` is a small recursive deep-equal on JSON values.
+- Errors: a dedicated `JsonPatchError` extending `Error`, mirroring `JsonPointerError`; pointer errors propagate as they are.
+- Assumption: removing the root (`""`) is an error, since the RFC leaves no representable result.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- Cloning is O(document size) per call; acceptable for the intended use and simpler than structural sharing.
