@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+## Why
+
+Our services need to change JSON documents with standard patches instead of ad-hoc update code. RFC 6902 (JSON Patch) is the published standard, and the library already provides RFC 6901 pointers it builds on.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `applyPatch(document, patch)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, implementing RFC 6902 with the operations `add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy` and `test`.
+- It returns the patched document as a new value; the input document and patch are never mutated.
+- It throws an error when the patch is invalid or an operation fails; no partial result is returned.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `json-patch`: applying an RFC 6902 JSON Patch to a JSON document.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+<!-- none: json-pointer requirements are unchanged -->
+
+## Impact
+
+- New `src/patch.ts` and tests; one new export in `src/index.ts`.
+- Reuses the pointer parsing of `src/pointer.ts` (to be exposed internally). No new dependencies, no breaking changes.
